course: dictionary
lesson: 15456
title: Stimulated and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Stimulated» is the past form of the verb «stimulate». It tells you that something was made more active, or started or grew. The word family stimulate, stimulates, stimulating and stimulated all share the same root, so once you know one, you can work out the others.
explain: «The loud music stimulated the crowd to dance.» The music made the crowd start moving. The clues are music, crowd and dance, and they tell you stimulated means made to become active or excited.
explain: A person can be stimulated too. «The children felt stimulated by the science museum.» Their minds were interested, excited and full of ideas. Swap in the words «excited and curious» and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Stimulate» means to make something more active, or to make it start or grow.
fact: «Stimulated» can describe a person whose mind is interested, excited and full of ideas.
fact: In science, a nerve, muscle or sense is stimulated when something triggers it to react, like light stimulating the eye.
fact: «Over-stimulated» means given too much noise and excitement, and it is often said of babies or pets.
fact: A good check is to swap in «made more active» or «excited» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The new puzzle stimulated Amara's mind.» What does stimulated mean here? | *Made her mind active and interested | Made it fall asleep | Put it away in a box | Made it very cold
exercise: Find and copy the word that is the past form of stimulate. | stimulating | stimulate | *stimulated | stimulates
exercise: Why might a teacher want her pupils to be stimulated? | *So they are curious and full of ideas | So they go home early | So they forget the lesson | So they sit still and say nothing
test: «The warm sunshine stimulated the seeds to grow.» What does stimulated mean here? | Stopped them from growing | Made them go cold | *Made them start to grow | Buried them deep in the soil
test: Ben said he was stimulated by the story. What does this tell you? | He had lost his book | He felt sick after reading | *His mind was excited and full of ideas | He was tired and wanted to sleep
exam: «Too much noise and bright lights can over-stimulate a baby.» What does over-stimulate suggest? | Too little noise and a lot of sleep | *Too much noise and excitement | Nothing at all | Just the right amount of quiet
